import Lean.Elab.Command
import Tests.Compiler.OneOutWKeccakFTest
import Tools.ShippingMachineDepthCommandR

/-! # The Keccak sponge's depth endpoint by the OLD command name, after the switch (round par/b-23)

WRITTEN, NOT BUILT. TARGET-ONLY, HEAVY (the grouped loop took 454–489 s on
the sponge in the built runs; 3 GiB cap, peak ≈ 2.6 GiB resident there).
NOT in `Tests/AllTests.lean`.

`Tests/Compiler/NoPortsKeccakSpongeTest.lean` (built) generates the sponge's
base depth endpoint by `#machine_design_svNRG … 1 as_old`, that is by the
loop of `Tools/ShippingMachineDepthCommandRG.lean`. That file is unchanged
by round par/b-23, so the built sponge test keeps passing whatever the
switch did and does NOT exercise the switched command. This file does: it
runs

    #machine_design_svNR keccak256SpongeHW 1

— the old command, whose `generateCoreNR` is now the grouped loop of
`Tools/ShippingMachineDepthCommandR.lean` — in the closure of
`OneOutWKeccakFTest` (the callee's theorems, as in the built sponge test),
and asserts that the three theorems exist under the OLD names. The
generator's `addTheorem` has kernel-checked each and tested its axioms; the
axiom test is repeated here on the composed theorem.

It logs the fingerprints (`Expr.hash` of the type, number of leading
binders) of the three statements, for comparison BY THE READER with those of
`keccak256SpongeHW.machine_*NR1` in a build of `NoPortsKeccakSpongeTest`
(there the old names are added by `as_old`: the composed theorem is another
name of the `NRG` one, the two others are built by the old
`generateDesignNR`). Nothing is asserted about that comparison: the two
files cannot be imported together.

NAME CLASH: this file, `NoPortsKeccakSpongeTest` and the Keccak probes all
generate `keccak256SpongeHW.*`; never import two of them together.

SCOPE: one declaration, depth 1; the base endpoint WITH its four check
premises (`shipsHierCheck`, `kidsMaskedN`, `designCheck`, `outsCheck`) —
this file removes none of them and says nothing of the check-free
endpoint, of the SV string or of `#sim`.

    SPARKLE_MACHINE_PROGRESS=$HOME/sparkle-work/sponge-switch.log \
      ~/sparkle-work/bin/cgrun.sh -n sponge-switch -m 3G -s 0 -t 2400 -- \
      lake build Tests.Compiler.DepthSwitchSpongeTest
-/

run_cmd Lean.Elab.Command.liftCoreM do
  let f := ``Sparkle.IP.Crypto.Keccak256Sponge.keccak256SpongeHW
  let env ← Lean.getEnv
  for n in [f ++ `machine_sound, f ++ `machine_composedNR1, f ++ `machine_composedNRG1,
      f ++ `machine_ships_hierNR1, f ++ `machine_design_svNR1] do
    if env.contains n then
      throwError "{n}: exists already — a Keccak probe or NoPortsKeccakSpongeTest is imported (NAME CLASH, see the header)"

set_option maxHeartbeats 0 in
#machine_endpoint Sparkle.IP.Crypto.Keccak256Sponge.keccak256SpongeHW

set_option maxHeartbeats 0 in
#machine_design_svNR Sparkle.IP.Crypto.Keccak256Sponge.keccak256SpongeHW 1

namespace Tests.Compiler.DepthSwitchSpongeTest

/-- The number of leading binders of a statement. -/
partial def binderCount : Lean.Expr → Nat
  | Lean.Expr.forallE _ _ b _ => binderCount b + 1
  | Lean.Expr.mdata _ e => binderCount e
  | _ => 0

end Tests.Compiler.DepthSwitchSpongeTest

set_option maxHeartbeats 0 in
run_cmd Lean.Elab.Command.liftCoreM do
  let f := ``Sparkle.IP.Crypto.Keccak256Sponge.keccak256SpongeHW
  let env ← Lean.getEnv
  let mut lines : List String := []
  for n in [f ++ `machine_composedNR1, f ++ `machine_ships_hierNR1, f ++ `machine_design_svNR1] do
    match env.find? n with
    | some (Lean.ConstantInfo.thmInfo ti) =>
      lines := lines ++ [s!"{n}: hash {ti.type.hash.toNat}, {Tests.Compiler.DepthSwitchSpongeTest.binderCount ti.type} binders"]
    | _ => throwError "{n}: not generated as a theorem by #machine_design_svNR"
  -- the grouped names must NOT have been produced by the old command
  for n in [f ++ `machine_composedNRG1, f ++ `machine_ships_hierNRG1, f ++ `machine_design_svNRG1] do
    if env.contains n then throwError "{n}: exists — the old command must add the NR names only"
  for ax in ← Lean.collectAxioms (f ++ `machine_composedNR1) do
    unless ax == ``propext || ax == ``Classical.choice || ax == ``Quot.sound do
      throwError "{f}.machine_composedNR1 uses a non-standard axiom: {ax}"
  Lean.logInfo m!"DEPTH SWITCH SPONGE: {f} — machine_composedNR1, machine_ships_hierNR1, machine_design_svNR1 generated by the OLD command #machine_design_svNR (its loop is the grouped one of Tools/ShippingMachineDepthCommandR.lean), kernel-checked, standard axioms. Fingerprints: {lines}. SCOPE: one declaration, depth 1, the base endpoint with its four check premises; no premise removed"
